- Fuel subsidy removal was a deliberate stabilization choice, not a passive outcome.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan further removes fuel subsidies to win IMF funding","publisher":"Reuters / Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/pakistan-further-removes-fuel-subsidies-to-win-imf-funding-finance-minister-2837532","claim":"Finance Minister Miftah Ismail said the government ended fuel subsidies and raised prices to trim the fiscal deficit and secure IMF support.","locator":"article lead and summary paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous report on a directly announced policy shift.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"June 2022, directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct policy choice under Sharif; it also unwound an inherited subsidy package.","contrary_evidence":["The move was inflationary and politically costly.","It mainly reversed a predecessor policy rather than creating new prosperity."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

